==============================================================================
S4  Complete-assay leave-one-out: can baseline context predict magnitude?
==============================================================================
   held-out unit = complete assay (['assay_1', 'assay_2', 'assay_3']); each fold predicts all 6 cells of one assay from the other two assays
   pred_assay_invariant   MAE_FC=0.3398 RMSE_FC=0.3930 bias=+0.0203 pooled rho=-0.586
   pred_level_transfer    MAE_FC=0.5688 RMSE_FC=0.7626 bias=-0.1874 pooled rho=-0.228
   pred_rank_transfer     MAE_FC=0.3780 RMSE_FC=0.4394 bias=-0.0030 pooled rho=-0.484
   within-assay compartment ordering (Spearman over 3 compartments, 6 folds):
      rank-transfer  mean rho = +0.250 per-fold [1.0, 0.5, 0.5, -0.5, 1.0, -1.0]
      level-transfer mean rho = +0.250 per-fold [1.0, 0.5, 0.5, -0.5, 1.0, -1.0]
   NOTE: training-set baseline spans 0.43 decades between assays, so a pooled log10(baseline) model is dominated by assay identity rather than by the within-assay compartment contrast.

